echo "== GAP-044: the writer gap for REF-01002's author row =="
python3 scripts/db.py add-gap --category SW --priority P2 --skill governance --session "$S" \
 --description "A KNOWN-WRONG AUTHOR ROW THAT NO SANCTIONED WRITER CAN CORRECT. REF-01002's fourth author is stored as 'Weiner, Jerome M.' (from TRID, a record GAP-026 already showed wrong on its publisher field). The publisher's own table of contents for J Architectural and Planning Research 26(2), Summer 2009 -- lockescience.com/TOC262.pdf, persisted in the batch-20 retrieval log as 07da0016d338f0f8.pdf, a born-digital text PDF (no page images; embedded Times New Roman), rendered and read -- prints 'Jerome M. Welner'. THE ROW CANNOT BE FIXED: correct-source REFUSES DOI-less sources ('no DOI, so no payload can be keyed to it'), its payload map reads only Crossref-shaped JSON, and it is the only verb that rewrites an admitted source's author rows (add-source writes them once, at admission); CLAUDE.md section 4 forbids hand SQL on a table the CLI should reach. That is a coverage bug, not a licence to bypass. WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN ONE LETTER: the corpus's signature failure (2026-08-19) was a wrong author list that six gates passed; here the right name is in hand, persisted and rendered, and the wrong one stays because the correction path only trusts DOI-keyed payloads. Grey and pre-DOI sources -- REF-01005, REF-01008, every T5/T6 row -- have the same exposure. WHAT WOULD CLOSE IT: let correct-source take a persisted non-Crossref artefact (a publisher TOC, a title page render) with an explicit field map and its own verify-authors comparison, then correct REF-01002 through it. Derive the row's state rather than trusting this text: select position, last_name, first_name from evidence_source_authors where ref_id='REF-01002'." 2>&1 | tail -3

echo "== GAP-033: adjudication has run =="
python3 scripts/db.py amend-gap --gap-id GAP-033 --session "$S" --append-note "BATCH 20: ADJUDICATION HAS RUN OVER THE WHOLE BACKLOG, AND THIS GAP STAYS OPEN ONLY FOR WHAT WAS DEFERRED WITH A REASON. Every observed_terms row now carries a term_adjudications row, each with an observation-specific rationale. DERIVE THE COUNTS, DO NOT QUOTE THEM: select outcome, count(*) from term_adjudications group by outcome; and the residual backlog: select count(*) from observed_terms o where not exists (select 1 from term_adjudications a where a.observation_id=o.observation_id). SIX TERMS WERE MINTED through add-term (NAMES-NEW), each warranted by the corpus rather than coined: ramp (the element; TERM-001 is its slope), level difference, ramp run length, intermediate landing, ramp usability (the outcome side: completion, Borg effort, discomfort and difficulty ratings are adjudicated to it as measures), and accessibility audit -- derive them with select term_id, canonical_en from terms where created_by_session like '%batch-20%'. THE DEFERRALS GROUP INTO FIVE OPEN QUESTIONS, and each is a decision about the vocabulary, not about a phrase: (1) RAMP VERSUS ROUTE GRADIENT -- TERM-001 is defined on ramps, four observations measure path and trail slopes, and extraction 49 already files REF-01003's path slopes on parameter 3; this is a scoping question for parameter 3 itself and belongs to the batch that re-determines it. (2) ACTIVITY PHRASES (ascending slopes, slope propulsion) -- term rows or ICF d4 links; the only activity-shaped terms are the functional-axis rows the owner called a bad coinage on 2026-08-18. (3) CONCEPTS HELD AS COLUMN VOCABULARIES (self-propulsion as device_class, CBPR as co1_source_type) -- rule 5 forbids a second home as a term, and NOT-OURS would be false. (4) THE DESIGN CASE (marginal population) -- the project's answer is the owner's most-accommodating rule, a doctrine, which a term would smuggle into the vocabulary. (5) SINGLE-SOURCE OR BACK-TRANSLATION RISKS (accessible route from a Japanese statute, site path, dwelling setting, a named housing standard, universal accessibility from a title, ramp incident, exterior ramp threshold) -- each needs a source that states the concept in its own words. PREDICTION TESTED: prior P5a (a writer or vocabulary defect surfaces before the verb runs cleanly) was NOT borne out -- adjudicate-term and add-term ran cleanly on every row." 2>&1 | tail -2
